  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since,&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>f</mi></math> is not one-one<br />Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> to be real, <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> <math><mi>y</mi></math> is neither equal to <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> nor <math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Range of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8713;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is into function</p>"
